Template: bbb-plugin-rtt-monitor/set-lastentriescap
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Enable a full 10-minute RTT history?
 The monitor backfills its graph from BigBlueButton's connection-status
 history, which by default keeps only the last 20 samples per user
 (~3 minutes at the ~10-second probe cadence). For a full 10 minutes of
 history to appear the instant a moderator opens the panel, the cap
 public.stats.lastEntriesCap must be raised.
 .
 If you accept, public.stats.lastEntriesCap will be set to 64 (~10.5 min)
 in /etc/bigbluebutton/bbb-html5.yml. A BigBlueButton restart is required
 for it to take effect; this package will NOT restart BigBlueButton for
 you (that would disconnect any live meeting) — it only prints a reminder.
 .
 Decline to leave the cap unchanged: the monitor still works, it just
 fills its window over the first few minutes the panel is open instead of
 showing the full history immediately.
